INT. BACK ROOM OF A BAR - NIGHT

low light, mismatched chairs. a long table. four people who have only ever typed to each other.

jonah kasprzak, 30s, in a faded army jacket, gets there first. he turns a phone over and over in his hand.

CLOSE ON the phone. a group chat. the name at the top reads: BRAVO 6 (reunion?).

odalys pierce, 40, walks in wearing scrubs and a heavy coat. she stops. looks at him.

ODALYS
you're boots.

JONAH
you're mama bear.

ODALYS
yeah. oh my god. hi.

they hug, awkward, too long. behind them, tamsin, 20s, with a shaved head and a trembling duffel, hovers in the doorway.

TAMSIN
is this the. is this where

JONAH
yeah come in, come in

TAMSIN
okay. cool. i'm tams. i'm. yeah.

ODALYS
tams! the kid who sent the ramen pics

TAMSIN
that was in basic. that was a long time ago

ANGLE ON the door. rafe oyelaran, 50, sixty pounds heavier than any photo, leans on a cane. nobody says anything.

RAFE
well. don't everybody get up.

JONAH
(standing)
sarge

RAFE
jonah. sit down. i'm not your sarge in a bar.

ODALYS
rafe, you look

RAFE
like hell. yes.

everyone laughs, a little too hard. chairs scrape. nobody quite sits.

TAMSIN
i didn't think i'd come. i almost didn't. i was in the car for like an hour

ODALYS
we all did that

JONAH
i drove past twice

RAFE
three times.

JONAH
you were here?

RAFE
i was in the lot.

this is the first time in nine years all four of them are in a room. none of them knows how to say what they mean.

ODALYS
so. who's ordering. because i need a drink and i need somebody to say something about the chat

TAMSIN
the chat

RAFE
the thing in march

JONAH
(quietly)
we don't have to

ODALYS
yes we do. jonah. that's the whole reason

a long pause. a glass clinks somewhere in the bar. tamsin sits first, then the others.

TAMSIN
okay. so. i'll start
